{
  "ok": true,
  "factory": {
    "id": "fac_platform",
    "name": "Platform team",
    "description": "The database engineer changes the schema with migrations, the backend developer builds on it, then security and testing review in parallel; anything blocking goes back to the developers, and DevOps makes sure it builds and runs.",
    "version": 3,
    "createdAt": "2026-10-20T09:00:00.000Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-10-23T18:30:00.000Z",
    "settings": {
      "managerMode": "normal",
      "mergeMode": "ask",
      "setupCommand": "",
      "autoRecover": false,
      "teamMode": "ask",
      "presets": [
        "git-read",
        "tests"
      ],
      "rules": [],
      "managerRules": true,
      "crTemplate": [
        {
          "id": "goal",
          "label": "Goal",
          "hint": "Why this change, and what it should achieve. One or two sentences.",
          "required": true,
          "list": false
        },
        {
          "id": "current",
          "label": "Current situation",
          "hint": "What exists or happens today, and what is wrong or missing. For a new project: what there is to start from.",
          "required": false,
          "list": false
        },
        {
          "id": "expected",
          "label": "Expected result",
          "hint": "What it should do when finished: behaviour, screens, data, APIs. Concrete examples help.",
          "required": true,
          "list": false
        },
        {
          "id": "done",
          "label": "Done when",
          "hint": "One check per line. The reviewers hold the work to these, and the Manager finishes only when they all pass.",
          "required": true,
          "list": true
        },
        {
          "id": "scope",
          "label": "Out of scope",
          "hint": "What not to do or touch, one per line.",
          "required": false,
          "list": true
        },
        {
          "id": "notes",
          "label": "Constraints and references",
          "hint": "Tech to use or avoid, conventions, links, anything the team should know.",
          "required": false,
          "list": false
        }
      ],
      "limits": {
        "pauseAt5h": 100,
        "pauseAtWeek": 100,
        "maxParallel": 0,
        "oneAtATimeAbove": 0
      },
      "tickMinutes": 0,
      "gatekeeper": {
        "enabled": false,
        "model": "haiku"
      },
      "caps": {
        "maxHandoffs": 200,
        "maxMinutes": 480,
        "tokenBudget": 0
      }
    },
    "roster": [
      {
        "id": "manager",
        "name": "Manager",
        "persona": "You lead the team like a good engineering manager: you make sure the change request is understood before work starts (ask the person when it is not), give each person what they need, keep the work moving, and only finish when every \"Done when\" check is met and the reviewers are satisfied. When something goes wrong you decide; you do not do the work yourself.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": []
        },
        "skills": [],
        "presets": []
      },
      {
        "id": "db",
        "name": "Database engineer",
        "persona": "You own the data: schema, migrations, indexes and queries. Every schema change is a migration that can run on existing data and be rolled back; you never drop or rewrite data without saying so in your handoff. Check query plans for anything that will grow, keep constraints in the database rather than only in code, and seed or fixture data the others need. Write the data model to the shared folder as data.md when you change it.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": []
        },
        "skills": [
          "crundi"
        ],
        "presets": [
          "tests"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "be",
        "name": "Backend dev",
        "persona": "You are a backend developer. You change server code and APIs carefully: validate input, keep existing behaviour working, return clear errors, and add or update tests for what you touch. Keep changes focused on the change request and follow the plan in the shared folder if there is one.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": []
        },
        "skills": [
          "crundi"
        ],
        "presets": []
      },
      {
        "id": "sec",
        "name": "Security reviewer",
        "persona": "You look for security problems in the change: injection, missing authorisation, secrets in code or logs, unsafe file or shell access, and data exposed to people who should not see it. File each as a finding with where it is and how to fix it. You do not edit code.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "fresh",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": [
            "Edit",
            "Write",
            "MultiEdit",
            "NotebookEdit"
          ]
        },
        "skills": [],
        "presets": []
      },
      {
        "id": "qa",
        "name": "Tester",
        "persona": "You test the change against the change request's \"Done when\" checks. Run the project's tests and write new ones for the behaviour it adds; for anything with an interface, drive it in a real browser. Try the obvious ways it could break. Report what you ran and what failed, with the exact output, as findings.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": []
        },
        "skills": [
          "crundi"
        ],
        "presets": [
          "tests",
          "packages"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ops",
        "name": "DevOps engineer",
        "persona": "You make it run: build scripts, configuration, containers, CI and how it is started and checked on this machine. Use free high ports, never the reserved ones, and register long-running processes as Crundi services rather than leaving them in a shell. Leave a short RUNNING.md in the shared folder: how to start it, check it and stop it.",
        "model": "",
        "effort": "",
        "memory": "keep",
        "tools": {
          "allow": [],
          "deny": []
        },
        "skills": [
          "crundi"
        ],
        "presets": [
          "tests",
          "packages"
        ]
      }
    ],
